      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>What size excavator do I need for a pool?</h3>
      <p>A 5.5T excavator is the most common choice for standard residential pool excavation in Sydney (8m × 4m). For larger pools or difficult access, a 3.5T may be used in tight spaces. The 5.5T provides the digging depth (3,800mm), bucket capacity (0.21m³), and power to complete a standard pool excavation efficiently.</p>
      <h3>What size excavator do I need for a house footing?</h3>
      <p>For standard residential footings (600mm wide, up to 900mm deep), a 1.7T or 3.5T mini excavator is sufficient. For deeper footings over 900mm or wider than 600mm, a 5.5T provides the extra reach and power needed.</p>
      <h3>What size excavator do I need for landscaping?</h3>
      <p>For residential landscaping — retaining walls, garden beds, drainage, and small earthworks — a 1T or 1.7T mini excavator is ideal. For larger landscaping jobs with significant earthmoving, a 3.5T or 5.5T is more productive.</p>
